crypto-eip: make mtk_crypto_zero_hmac_setkey static

Building with CRYPTO_MTK_DDK_LOOKASIDE=y and CRYPTO_OFFLOAD_INLINE=y at the
same time fails:

  lookaside-hash.c:599:5: error: no previous prototype for
      'mtk_crypto_zero_hmac_setkey' [-Werror=missing-prototypes]

The function is defined at line 599 and used once, at line 712, in the same
file.  Nothing outside lookaside-hash.c references it and no header declares
it, so static is the right fix.

The two config symbols are independent in Config.in (CRYPTO_MTK_DDK_LOOKASIDE
sits outside the "Crypto Offload Mode" choice), but the combination appears
never to be built by MediaTek - lookaside-hash.c is only compiled when the
look-aside symbol is set, and the module it lands in is crypto-eip-inline.ko.

--- a/feed/kernel/crypto-eip/src/lookaside-hash.c
+++ b/feed/kernel/crypto-eip/src/lookaside-hash.c
@@ -596,7 +596,7 @@
 	return crypto_ahash_export(areq, state);
 }
 
-int mtk_crypto_zero_hmac_setkey(const char *alg, const u8 *key, unsigned int keylen,
+static int mtk_crypto_zero_hmac_setkey(const char *alg, const u8 *key, unsigned int keylen,
 			   void *istate)
 {
 	struct ahash_request *areq;
